            "current": "Why we review every table change"
          },
          "title": "Why we review every table change",
          "author": {
            "name": "Maren Foxley",
            "avatar": {
              "assetRole": "person.fictional-avatar",
              "alt": "",
              "ref": "generate:avatar-1"
            },
            "href": "#"
          },
          "date": "Last edited on March 3, 2027"
        },
        "blocks": [
          {
            "kind": "p",
            "text": "Small teams often skip review for data changes because a table feels less risky than an application. That habit holds until the first dashboard quietly shows the wrong total."
          },
          {
            "kind": "h2",
            "text": "What a review catches"
          },
          {
            "kind": "p",
            "text": "A second reader notices renamed columns, joins that multiply rows and filters that silently drop a region. None of these fail a build, yet each one changes a number somebody reports upward."
          },
          {
            "kind": "ul",
            "items": [
              {
                "text": "A before and after row count for every changed table."
              },
              {
                "text": "A named owner for each table who can answer questions."
              },
              {
                "text": "A short note on why the change was made."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "kind": "h2",
            "text": "Keeping it light"
          },
          {
            "kind": "p",
            "text": "Reviews stay quick when changes are small and previews show real results. Aim for a few minutes of reading, not a meeting."
          },
          {
            "kind": "p",
            "text": "A review is cheaper than a retraction."
          }
        ],
        "promos": [
          {
            "title": "Try a sample project",
            "body": "Open a free workspace with a small project that already has review checks switched on.",
            "cta": {
              "label": "Open the sample",
              "href": "/signup"
            }
          },
          {
            "title": "Read the field guide",
            "body": "A practical guide to planning, reviewing and releasing analytics work as a small team.",
            "cta": {
              "label": "Get the guide",
              "href": "/guides/field-guide"
            }
          }
        ]
      },
